# EAS Build reads this file INSTEAD of .gitignore when deciding which
# files to upload. This repo is a monorepo, so by default EAS uploaded
# the whole thing (~158 MB). We only build the Expo apps (customer-app,
# staff-app), so exclude the heavy, unrelated parts of the repo.
#
# NOTE: because this replaces .gitignore, we must also re-exclude
# node_modules and caches here, or they would get uploaded.

# --- Reinstalled / regenerated on the build server ---
**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/dist/
# Any dist-* scratch export. Named individually before, so a new one
# (dist-driver-check, 13 MB) went into the upload unnoticed.
**/dist-*/
**/web-build/
/.git/
.git/
.claude/
**/.eas-archive-inspect/
/staff-app/.eas-archive-inspect/
/staff-app/.eas-archive-inspect/**

# --- Monorepo parts not needed to build the mobile apps ---
/tmp/
/public/
/src/
/supabase/
/whatsapp-bot/
/old whatsapp bots/
/store-assets/
/poster-output/
/deliverables/
/output/
/docs/
/scripts/
/tools/
/.github/

# --- Monorepo release material, excluded RECURSIVELY ---
#
# These were previously listed only as root-anchored paths (/deliverables/),
# but EAS evaluates the per-app .easignore from the app directory, where a
# leading slash means the app folder and not the repo root. So none of them
# matched and every build uploaded a 255 MB archive: deliverables is 408 MB,
# public 90 MB, tmp 54 MB, store-assets 17 MB. That is not merely slow — a
# 1.1.5 APK build died at 102 MB of 255 MB with write ECONNRESET, because the
# bigger the upload the likelier it is to be reset.
#
# Only names that do NOT exist inside an app folder are globbed. `src`,
# `scripts` and `assets` are deliberately absent from this list: staff-app has
# all three, and `**/src/` would exclude the app's own source.
**/deliverables/
**/public/
**/tmp/
**/store-assets/
**/poster-output/
**/output/
**/docs/
**/tools/
**/supabase/
**/whatsapp-bot/
**/old whatsapp bots/
